{"drafts":[{"assumptions":["ASM-13 is used over ASM-5: 'cannot be delivered' means only an immediate error from the mail service. ASM-5 (high risk, bounce webhooks) contradicts it and needs confirming by the product owner before build.","ASM-12 is used over ASM-5 for the provider: sending sits behind a mail-service interface with SMTP as the default, so tests use a stub for that interface.","'7 days past due' means the calendar days from due date to today in the business time zone are ≥ threshold, so an invoice due 2026-10-08 is overdue on 2026-10-15 (ASM-2, ASM-10, ASM-11).","ASM-4's '60+' bucket is read as 61+ so it does not overlap the 31–60 bucket; limits are inclusive.","A send blocked by a missing billing email counts as an attempt and is logged as failed (Q-8, ASM-6).","Amounts are shown in GBP with a £ symbol, from the fixed template in ASM-9/ASM-15; the date format in the email is set in config.","Invoices, customers, billing emails and paid/cancelled status are read from the client's existing Postgres database (ASM-1); reminder history is a new table in that database keyed by invoice ID (Q-7).","Endpoint paths are left to design; tests call the overdue list, invoice detail and send reminder endpoints of the existing .NET 8 API.","Today's date is supplied by an injectable clock so tests can fix it."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"p95 ≤ 1,000 ms for a list query over 5,000 open invoices, measured at the API","text":"Overdue list response time with filters applied"},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"The mail service call times out after 10 s; on timeout the attempt is recorded as failed (REQ-10) and the API responds within 12 s","text":"Send reminder endpoint waits a bounded time for the mail service"},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"0 occurrences of customer email addresses in application log output across the REQ-4, REQ-5 and REQ-10 test runs","text":"PII protection: customer billing email addresses and invoice amounts are kept out of application logs"},{"id":"NFR-4","metric":"100% of new Invoice Reminders endpoints return 401 without valid credentials (checked by an automated endpoint sweep)","text":"Authentication coverage"},{"id":"NFR-5","metric":"0 history rows lost or changed after 1,000 back-to-back send attempts, including 100 forced mail-service failures","text":"Reminder history durability"}],"outOfScope":["Payments and recording payments (invoice status is only read from the existing system)","Customer logins or customer-facing screens","SMS reminders","Bounce/complaint webhooks and later delivery failures (only immediate mail-service errors count as failures, per ASM-13)","Automatic or scheduled reminders; every send is started by staff","Server-side duplicate-send throttling beyond disabling the button during a send (Q-5)","Role-based permissions beyond 'authenticated staff user' (Q-1)","Creating or editing invoices, customers or billing emails","Sending to more than one contact per customer","Storing an 'overdue' status on the invoice or a daily job to set it (Q-6)"],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"threshold is the default 7, today in the business time zone is 2026-10-15, and an open invoice INV-1 has due date 2026-10-08","id":"AC-1.1","level":"api","then":"INV-1 is in the response with daysOverdue = 7","when":"an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list"},{"given":"threshold is 7, today is 2026-10-15, and an open invoice INV-2 has due date 2026-10-09","id":"AC-1.2","level":"api","then":"INV-2 is not in the response","when":"an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list"},{"given":"today is 2026-10-15, invoice INV-3 has due date 2026-09-01 and status paid, and invoice INV-4 has due date 2026-09-01 and status cancelled","id":"AC-1.3","level":"api","then":"neither INV-3 nor INV-4 is in the response","when":"an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list"},{"given":"the overdue threshold is set to 10, today is 2026-10-15, and an open invoice INV-5 has due date 2026-10-07","id":"AC-1.4","level":"api","then":"INV-5 is not in the response","when":"an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list"},{"given":"the overdue invoice INV-1 was in the overdue list and its status in the existing system is then changed to paid","id":"AC-1.5","level":"api","then":"INV-1 is not in the response, and no overdue flag was stored on the invoice row","when":"an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list again"},{"given":"an overdue invoice INV-1 for customer 'Crumb & Co' with amount 125.50 and due date 2026-10-01, with today 2026-10-15","id":"AC-1.6","level":"api","then":"the INV-1 entry holds invoice number INV-1, customer 'Crumb & Co', amount 125.50, due date 2026-10-01 and daysOverdue 14","when":"an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list"}],"ears":"The Invoice Reminders API shall include an invoice in the overdue list only when its status in the existing system is neither paid nor cancelled and the number of calendar days from its due date to today's date in the business time zone is at least the configured overdue threshold (default 7).","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-4","Q-6","ASM-1","ASM-2","ASM-10","ASM-11"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"customer A has overdue invoices INV-10 and INV-11 and customer B has overdue invoice INV-12","id":"AC-2.1","level":"api","then":"the response holds INV-10 and INV-11 and does not hold INV-12","when":"an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list filtered by customer A"},{"given":"customer C exists and has no overdue invoices","id":"AC-2.2","level":"api","then":"the response is an empty list with a success status","when":"an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list filtered by customer C"}],"ears":"When the overdue list is requested with a customer filter, the Invoice Reminders API shall return only overdue invoices belonging to that customer.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"overdue invoices exist with 7, 30, 31, 60 and 61 days since their due dates","id":"AC-3.1","level":"api","then":"only the invoices with 7 and 30 days are returned","when":"an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list with bucket 7–30"},{"given":"the same invoices","id":"AC-3.2","level":"api","then":"only the invoices with 31 and 60 days are returned","when":"an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list with bucket 31–60"},{"given":"the same invoices","id":"AC-3.3","level":"api","then":"only the invoice with 61 days is returned","when":"an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list with bucket 61+"},{"given":"customer A has overdue invoices at 10 and 45 days and customer B has an overdue invoice at 10 days","id":"AC-3.4","level":"api","then":"only customer A's 10-day invoice is returned","when":"an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list filtered by customer A and bucket 7–30"}],"ears":"When the overdue list is requested with a days-overdue bucket filter of 7–30, 31–60 or 61+, the Invoice Reminders API shall return only overdue invoices whose days since due date fall inside that bucket, inclusive of both limits.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","ASM-3","ASM-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"overdue invoice INV-1 (amount 125.50, due date 2026-10-01) whose customer has billing email accounts@crumb.example, and a stub mail service that accepts messages","id":"AC-4.1","level":"api","then":"the stub mail service receives exactly one message addressed only to accounts@crumb.example, from the configured sender address, whose body contains 'INV-1', '£125.50' and '1 October 2026' (or the configured local date format), and the API returns a success status","when":"an authenticated staff user sends a reminder for INV-1"}],"ears":"When an authenticated staff user requests a reminder for an overdue invoice whose customer has a billing email, the Invoice Reminders API shall send one email through the mail service to that billing email containing the invoice number, the amount in local currency and the due date.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","Q-1","Q-2","ASM-9","ASM-12","ASM-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"overdue invoice INV-20 whose customer has an empty billing email, and a stub mail service","id":"AC-5.1","level":"api","then":"the API returns a 4xx error whose message says the billing email is missing, the stub mail service receives no message, and one reminder history row for INV-20 exists with outcome 'failed' and reason 'missing billing email'","when":"an authenticated staff user sends a reminder for INV-20"}],"ears":"If a reminder is requested for an invoice whose customer has no billing email, then the Invoice Reminders API shall reject the request with an error stating the billing email is missing and send no email.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-2","Q-8","ASM-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"open invoice INV-30 that is 3 days past its due date, and a stub mail service","id":"AC-6.1","level":"api","then":"the API returns a 4xx error saying the invoice is not overdue and the stub mail service receives no message","when":"an authenticated staff user sends a reminder for INV-30"},{"given":"invoice INV-31 with status paid that is 40 days past its due date","id":"AC-6.2","level":"api","then":"the API returns a 4xx error and the stub mail service receives no message","when":"an authenticated staff user sends a reminder for INV-31"}],"ears":"If a reminder is requested for an invoice that is not in the overdue list under REQ-1, then the Invoice Reminders API shall reject the request with an error and send no email.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","Q-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"overdue invoice INV-1 with no reminder history and a stub mail service that accepts messages","id":"AC-7.1","level":"api","then":"the reminder history table holds exactly one row for INV-1 with sender 'jane', timestamp 2026-10-15T09:00:00Z (±5 s), outcome 'sent' and no failure reason","when":"staff user 'jane' sends a reminder for INV-1 at 2026-10-15T09:00:00Z"},{"given":"INV-1 already has one 'sent' history row","id":"AC-7.2","level":"api","then":"the table holds two rows for INV-1, the first row is unchanged, and the new row has sender 'tom'","when":"staff user 'tom' sends another reminder for INV-1"}],"ears":"When a reminder send attempt for an overdue invoice finishes, the Invoice Reminders API shall add one row to the reminder history table in Postgres holding the invoice ID, the sending staff user's ID, the UTC timestamp of the attempt, the outcome (sent or failed) and any failure reason.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-7","Q-8","ASM-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"INV-1 has a reminder history entry with a known ID","id":"AC-8.1","level":"api","then":"each request returns 404 or 405 and the history row in the database is unchanged","when":"an authenticated staff user sends PUT, PATCH and DELETE requests aimed at that history entry"}],"ears":"The Invoice Reminders API shall offer no operation that edits or deletes a reminder history entry.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"overdue invoice INV-1 with history rows: failed at 2026-10-10 (reason 'mail service error') by 'jane', then sent at 2026-10-12 by 'tom'","id":"AC-9.1","level":"api","then":"the response holds the amount, due date, overdue = true, the two history entries in order 2026-10-12 then 2026-10-10 each with sender, timestamp, outcome and reason, and latest outcome 'sent'","when":"an authenticated staff user requests INV-1's details"},{"given":"overdue invoice INV-2 whose only history row is 'failed' with reason 'mail service error'","id":"AC-9.2","level":"api","then":"latest outcome is 'failed' and the failure reason 'mail service error' is in the response","when":"an authenticated staff user requests INV-2's details"}],"ears":"When an authenticated staff user requests an invoice's details, the Invoice Reminders API shall return the invoice number, amount, due date, whether it is overdue, days overdue, its reminder history newest first, and the outcome of the latest reminder attempt.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-7","Q-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"overdue invoice INV-1 and a stub mail service configured to return an error","id":"AC-10.1","level":"api","then":"the API returns an error status saying the email could not be sent, a history row for INV-1 exists with outcome 'failed' and a non-empty reason, and a following overdue-list request still includes INV-1","when":"an authenticated staff user sends a reminder for INV-1"}],"ears":"If the mail service returns an error when a reminder is handed to it, then the Invoice Reminders API shall return an error to the caller, record the attempt as failed with the error reason, and keep the invoice in the overdue list.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","Q-8","ASM-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"no authentication credentials","id":"AC-11.1","level":"api","then":"each returns 401, no invoice data is in any response body, the stub mail service receives no message and no history row is added","when":"a client calls the overdue list, invoice detail and send reminder endpoints"},{"given":"a valid staff credential from the existing API with no special role","id":"AC-11.2","level":"api","then":"it returns 200","when":"the client calls the overdue list endpoint"}],"ears":"If a request to any Invoice Reminders endpoint is not authenticated through the existing API's authentication, then the Invoice Reminders API shall reject it with HTTP 401 and send no email.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"a signed-in staff user and three overdue invoices for two customers","id":"AC-12.1","level":"manual","then":"the table lists only that customer's invoices within 7–30 days, each row shows invoice number, customer, amount, due date, days overdue and a 'Send reminder' button, and clicking an invoice number opens that invoice's detail screen","when":"the user opens the overdue list screen, picks one customer, then picks bucket 7–30"}],"ears":"The overdue list screen shall show overdue invoices in a table with a customer filter, a days-overdue bucket filter, a 'Send reminder' button on each row, and a link from each row to the invoice detail screen.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-5","ASM-4","ASM-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"a signed-in staff user on the overdue list and a mail service slowed to respond after 5 seconds","id":"AC-13.1","level":"manual","then":"that button is disabled until the response arrives, then enabled again, and the screen shows the success or failure result","when":"the user presses 'Send reminder' on a row"}],"ears":"While a reminder send is in progress for an invoice, the React front end shall disable the 'Send reminder' button for that invoice.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-5","ASM-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"a signed-in staff user and an overdue invoice with one failed and one sent reminder","id":"AC-14.1","level":"manual","then":"the screen shows amount, due date, both history entries newest first with sender, time and outcome, the failure reason on the failed entry, the latest status, and an enabled 'Send reminder' button","when":"the user opens its detail screen"},{"given":"a signed-in staff user and an invoice that is not overdue","id":"AC-14.2","level":"manual","then":"no 'Send reminder' button is shown","when":"the user opens its detail screen"}],"ears":"The invoice detail screen shall show the invoice's amount, due date, reminder history with sender, time and outcome of each attempt, any delivery failure reasons, and, when the invoice is overdue, a 'Send reminder' button.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7","I-3","I-4","ASM-8","ASM-14"]}],"suggestions":["Confirm with the client whether later bounces should count as delivery failures (ASM-5 vs ASM-13); if yes, add a bounce webhook that appends a 'bounced' history entry.","Show the latest reminder date and outcome as columns on the overdue list so staff can see which invoices were already chased.","Consider a server-side guard (e.g. refuse a second send for the same invoice within 60 s) as the button-only guard does not stop sends from two browser tabs.","Add an audit log entry in the existing API's audit trail, if one exists, for each reminder sent.","Offer a 'no billing email' marker on the overdue list so staff can fix customer records before trying to send."]},{"assumptions":["ASM-1: Invoices, customers, billing emails and invoice status already exist in the client's .NET 8 API / Postgres database; this app reads them and only adds the reminder history table (Q-7).","ASM-2/ASM-10/ASM-11: The overdue threshold is a configuration setting, default 7. An invoice is overdue when today's local date in the configured business time zone minus the due date is at least the threshold.","ASM-3: 'Days overdue' means calendar days since the due date, not since the invoice became overdue.","ASM-4: Days-overdue buckets are 7–30, 31–60 and 61+, inclusive. The assumption's '60+' was changed to 61+ so the buckets do not overlap at 60. With a threshold other than 7, the lowest bucket still starts at 7 and may hold no invoices.","ASM-13 is used over ASM-5: they conflict, and ASM-13 answers the more specific question. Only immediate errors from the email sender (plus a missing billing email) count as 'cannot be delivered'. So ASM-6's 'bounced' outcome is not used and outcomes are 'sent' or 'failed'.","ASM-12 is used over ASM-5 for the provider: email goes through an email-sender interface with an SMTP default. Tests use a stub implementation of that interface as the outbound system.","ASM-9/ASM-15: The reminder uses a fixed plain template from a configured sender address, with the amount shown in local currency (GBP, e.g. '£245.50').","ASM-6/Q-8: A send blocked by a missing billing email also creates a 'failed' history entry.","Sending a reminder for an invoice that is not overdue (including paid or cancelled ones) is rejected with 409. This follows from I-2's 'on an overdue invoice'.","Endpoint paths and exact status codes (401, 409, 422, 400, 404/405) are fixed only as far as the acceptance criteria state. Route names are left to design."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"p95 response time ≤ 1000 ms with 5,000 open invoices and 20,000 reminder history rows","text":"The overdue list endpoint responds quickly with a realistic data volume, with or without filters."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"Email sender call timeout 10 s; endpoint response ≤ 12 s in 100% of calls; a timeout produces a 'failed' history row","text":"The send-reminder endpoint gives up on the email sender after a time limit and records the attempt as failed."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"0 occurrences of a test customer's billing email address in application log output across the full acceptance test run","text":"Customer billing emails (PII) are not written to application logs."},{"id":"NFR-4","metric":"0 UPDATE or DELETE statements against the reminder history table in application code (static check) and 0 changed rows across the test run","text":"Reminder history rows are never removed or modified by the application."}],"outOfScope":["Payments and payment recording (invoice paid/cancelled status is only read from the existing system)","Customer logins or any customer-facing screens","SMS reminders","Detecting later bounces or rejections via provider webhooks (only errors when the email is handed to the sender count as failures, per ASM-13)","Automatic or scheduled reminders; reminders are only sent when staff press the button","A stored 'overdue' status or daily job; overdue is computed at query time (Q-6)","Several contacts per customer; only the single billing email is used (Q-2)","Editing or deleting reminder history (Q-3)","Server-side duplicate-send protection beyond disabling the button (Q-5)","Role-based permissions beyond 'authenticated staff user' (Q-1)","Creating or editing invoices and customers (ASM-1)"],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"threshold 7, business time zone Europe/London, today 2026-10-15, an open invoice with due date 2026-10-08","id":"AC-1.1","level":"unit","then":"it returns overdue = true and daysOverdue = 7","when":"the overdue rule's public evaluation method is called with the invoice and today's date"},{"given":"threshold 7, today 2026-10-15, an open invoice with due date 2026-10-09","id":"AC-1.2","level":"unit","then":"it returns overdue = false","when":"the overdue rule is evaluated"},{"given":"threshold set to 10, today 2026-10-15, an open invoice with due date 2026-10-06 (9 days past due)","id":"AC-1.3","level":"unit","then":"it returns overdue = false; with due date 2026-10-05 it returns overdue = true","when":"the overdue rule is evaluated"},{"given":"threshold 7, an invoice 20 days past due whose existing status is paid (and a second one whose status is cancelled)","id":"AC-1.4","level":"unit","then":"both return overdue = false","when":"the overdue rule is evaluated for each"},{"given":"business time zone Europe/London, due date 2026-10-08, the evaluation instant is 2026-10-14T23:30Z (00:30 on 2026-10-15 local time)","id":"AC-1.5","level":"unit","then":"it uses local date 2026-10-15 and returns overdue = true","when":"the overdue rule is evaluated"}],"ears":"When the current calendar date in the configured business time zone is at least the configured overdue threshold (default 7) calendar days after an invoice's due date and the invoice's existing status is neither paid nor cancelled, the overdue rule shall classify the invoice as overdue at evaluation time.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-4","Q-6","ASM-2","ASM-10","ASM-11"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"today 2026-10-15, threshold 7, open invoices A (due 2026-10-01), B (due 2026-10-12) and C (due 2026-09-01, status paid) in the existing database","id":"AC-2.1","level":"api","then":"the response is 200 and contains only invoice A with daysOverdue = 14 plus its number, customer name, amount and due date","when":"GET on the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token"},{"given":"invoice A is on the overdue list","id":"AC-2.2","level":"api","then":"invoice A is no longer in the response, and no overdue flag is written to the invoice record","when":"its status in the existing system is changed to paid and the overdue list is requested again"},{"given":"overdue invoice A with no reminder attempts and overdue invoice D whose latest attempt failed","id":"AC-2.3","level":"api","then":"A has latest reminder outcome null and D has latest reminder outcome 'failed'","when":"the overdue list is requested"}],"ears":"When an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list, the API shall return every invoice currently classified as overdue, each with invoice ID, invoice number, customer name, amount, due date, days overdue (today minus due date) and latest reminder outcome.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-6","Q-4","Q-6","ASM-1","ASM-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"overdue invoices for customers X (2 invoices) and Y (1 invoice)","id":"AC-3.1","level":"api","then":"the response contains exactly the 2 invoices of customer X","when":"the overdue list is requested with customerId = X"},{"given":"customer Z exists and has no overdue invoices","id":"AC-3.2","level":"api","then":"the response is 200 with an empty list","when":"the overdue list is requested with customerId = Z"}],"ears":"When the overdue list is requested with a customer filter, the API shall return only overdue invoices belonging to that customer.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"overdue invoices with days overdue 7, 30, 31, 60 and 61","id":"AC-4.1","level":"api","then":"the responses contain {7, 30}, {31, 60} and {61} respectively","when":"the list is requested with bucket 7-30, then 31-60, then 61+"},{"given":"overdue invoices for customers X and Y, each with invoices at 10 and 45 days overdue","id":"AC-4.2","level":"api","then":"only customer X's 45-day invoice is returned","when":"the list is requested with customerId = X and bucket 31-60"},{"given":"any overdue invoices","id":"AC-4.3","level":"api","then":"the response is 400 with a validation error naming the bucket parameter","when":"the list is requested with an unknown bucket value such as '5-6'"}],"ears":"When the overdue list is requested with a days-overdue bucket of 7–30, 31–60 or 61+, the API shall return only overdue invoices whose days overdue fall inside that bucket, inclusive of both bounds.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","ASM-3","ASM-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"overdue invoice INV-1042, amount 245.50, due 2026-10-01, customer billing email accounts@bakery.example, and a stub email sender","id":"AC-5.1","level":"api","then":"the response is 2xx with outcome 'sent', and the stub email sender receives exactly one message to accounts@bakery.example from the configured sender address whose body contains 'INV-1042', '£245.50' and the due date 2026-10-01","when":"POST on the send-reminder endpoint for INV-1042 is called with a valid staff token"},{"given":"invoice INV-1050 is open but only 3 days past due (not overdue)","id":"AC-5.2","level":"api","then":"the response is 409 with an error saying the invoice is not overdue, and no email is handed to the email sender","when":"the send-reminder endpoint is called for it"}],"ears":"When an authenticated staff user requests a reminder for an overdue invoice whose customer has a billing email, the system shall send one email to that billing email containing the invoice number, the amount in local currency and the due date.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","Q-1","Q-2","ASM-9","ASM-12","ASM-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"an overdue invoice whose customer record has an empty billing email","id":"AC-6.1","level":"api","then":"the response is 422 with error code 'missing_billing_email', the stub email sender receives no message, and one reminder history row exists for the invoice with outcome 'failed' and reason 'missing billing email'","when":"the send-reminder endpoint is called with a valid staff token"}],"ears":"If a reminder is requested for an overdue invoice whose customer has no billing email, then the system shall reject the request with a 'missing billing email' error, send no email and record a history entry with outcome 'failed'.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-2","Q-8","ASM-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"staff user 'u-17' is authenticated and invoice INV-1042 is overdue with a working stub email sender","id":"AC-7.1","level":"api","then":"exactly one new reminder history row exists with invoice ID of INV-1042, staff user ID 'u-17', a UTC timestamp within 5 seconds of the call and outcome 'sent'","when":"u-17 calls the send-reminder endpoint for INV-1042"},{"given":"INV-1042 has already had one successful reminder","id":"AC-7.2","level":"api","then":"two history rows exist for INV-1042 and the first row is unchanged","when":"a second reminder is sent for it"}],"ears":"When a reminder send attempt finishes, the system shall add one row to the reminder history table in the Postgres database recording the invoice ID, the sending staff user's ID, the UTC timestamp of the attempt and the outcome ('sent' or 'failed') with any failure reason.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-7","Q-8","ASM-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"a reminder history entry exists for INV-1042","id":"AC-8.1","level":"api","then":"each response is 404 or 405, and the entry's row in the database is byte-for-byte unchanged","when":"PUT, PATCH or DELETE is sent to the path of that history entry with a valid staff token"}],"ears":"If a client requests to modify or delete a reminder history entry, then the API shall reject the request and leave the entry unchanged.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"overdue invoice INV-1042 and a stub email sender set to throw 'SMTP 554 rejected'","id":"AC-9.1","level":"api","then":"the response reports outcome 'failed' with reason containing 'SMTP 554 rejected', and a history row with outcome 'failed' and that reason is stored","when":"the send-reminder endpoint is called"},{"given":"the failed attempt in AC-9.1 has happened","id":"AC-9.2","level":"api","then":"INV-1042 is still in the list with latest reminder outcome 'failed'","when":"the overdue list is requested"}],"ears":"If the email sender returns an error when a reminder is handed to it, then the system shall return outcome 'failed' with the error reason to the caller, record the attempt as 'failed', and keep the invoice on the overdue list.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","Q-8","ASM-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"INV-1042 has attempts: 2026-10-10 failed by u-17 (reason 'SMTP 554'), then 2026-10-12 sent by u-20","id":"AC-10.1","level":"api","then":"the response has latest reminder outcome 'sent' and the history lists the 2026-10-12 entry (u-20, sent) first and the 2026-10-10 entry (u-17, failed, 'SMTP 554') second","when":"GET on the invoice detail endpoint for INV-1042 is called"},{"given":"INV-1042's only attempt failed","id":"AC-10.2","level":"api","then":"latest reminder outcome is 'failed' with its failure reason","when":"the invoice detail is requested"}],"ears":"When an authenticated staff user requests an invoice's details, the API shall return its invoice number, customer, amount, due date, overdue flag, days overdue, latest reminder outcome, and full reminder history newest first, with each entry's sender, timestamp, outcome and failure reason.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-4","I-7","Q-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"no token, and separately an expired token","id":"AC-11.1","level":"api","then":"each response is 401 with no invoice or customer data in the body, and the stub email sender receives no message","when":"the overdue list, invoice detail and send-reminder endpoints are called"},{"given":"a valid token for any staff user with no special role","id":"AC-11.2","level":"api","then":"none of them returns 401 or 403","when":"the same three endpoints are called for an overdue invoice"}],"ears":"If a request to any overdue-list, invoice-detail or send-reminder endpoint has no valid staff authentication from the existing API's authentication, then the API shall reject it with HTTP 401 without returning invoice data or sending email.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"a signed-in staff user and 3 overdue invoices for two customers","id":"AC-12.1","level":"ui","then":"the table shows invoice number, customer, amount, due date, days overdue and latest reminder outcome, narrows to matching rows after each filter, and every row has a 'Send reminder' button","when":"the person opens the overdue list screen, picks one customer, then picks bucket 31–60"},{"given":"the overdue list screen is showing INV-1042","id":"AC-12.2","level":"ui","then":"the invoice detail screen for INV-1042 opens","when":"the person clicks INV-1042's invoice number"}],"ears":"The overdue list screen shall show overdue invoices in a table with a customer filter, a days-overdue bucket filter, a 'Send reminder' button on each row, and a link from each row's invoice number to the invoice detail screen.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-6","ASM-4","ASM-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"overdue INV-1042 with one failed and one later successful attempt","id":"AC-13.1","level":"ui","then":"amount, due date, both history entries with sender, time and outcome, the failure reason on the failed entry, latest outcome 'sent' and a 'Send reminder' button are visible","when":"the person opens its detail screen"},{"given":"an invoice that is not overdue","id":"AC-13.2","level":"ui","then":"no 'Send reminder' button is shown","when":"the person opens its detail screen"}],"ears":"The invoice detail screen shall show the invoice's amount, due date, reminder history with sender, time and outcome, any delivery failure reasons, and a 'Send reminder' button while the invoice is overdue.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7","I-4","ASM-8","ASM-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"the email sender is slowed to take 5 seconds","id":"AC-14.1","level":"ui","then":"the button is disabled until the response arrives, only one history entry is created, and the button is enabled again afterwards with the new outcome shown","when":"the person presses 'Send reminder' on a row and presses it again within the 5 seconds"}],"ears":"While a reminder send for an invoice is in progress, the overdue list and invoice detail screens shall disable that invoice's 'Send reminder' button.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-5","I-6","ASM-14"]}],"suggestions":["Add provider bounce/complaint webhooks later (ASM-5), so late bounces show as failures on the invoice.","Add a server-side guard against duplicate sends, e.g. reject a second send for the same invoice within 60 seconds. At the moment only the button is disabled (Q-5), so two staff or two tabs can still send twice.","Consider limiting who can send reminders to a role, since any authenticated staff user can email customers.","Make the reminder email template and sender address editable by admins instead of fixed.","Show the configured overdue threshold on the overdue list screen, so staff know why a recently due invoice is missing.","Record which billing email address each reminder was sent to in the history row, as an audit trail if a customer's email changes later. Review this against PII retention first."]},{"assumptions":["Proposed API surface for the tests (new build, so no current names exist): GET /api/invoices/overdue?customerId=&daysOverdue={7-30|31-60|61+}, GET /api/invoices/{id}, POST /api/invoices/{id}/reminders. A reminder_history table stores invoice_id, sent_by, sent_at (UTC), status (sent|failed) and failure_reason. Day counting lives in one class, OverduePolicy, which takes an injected clock, the threshold and the time zone.","The email sender is an interface with an SMTP default implementation (ASM-12), so tests can swap in a fake. ASM-5 (a provider with bounce webhooks) conflicts with ASM-13 (immediate send errors only); this spec follows ASM-13 and leaves bounces out of scope. This needs confirming because ASM-5 is marked high risk.","ASM-4's buckets overlap at 60 (31–60 and 60+). This spec uses threshold–30, 31–60 and 61+. If the threshold is set above 30, the first bucket is empty.","ASM-2, ASM-10 and ASM-11 agree: the threshold defaults to 7 calendar days, can be configured, and days are counted from the due date in the business time zone (Europe/London is used in the examples). 'Overdue' means days since due date ≥ threshold.","A missing billing email is both blocked with an error (Q-2) and recorded as a failed attempt (Q-8, ASM-6). The status codes chosen are 422 for missing email, 409 for an invoice that is not overdue, and 502 for an email sender error.","Asking for a reminder on an invoice that is not overdue, paid or cancelled is rejected without a history entry, because I-2 limits sending to overdue invoices.","'Who sent it' is the user ID from the existing API's authentication token (Q-1).","A successful send does not take an invoice off the overdue list. Only a paid or cancelled status in the existing system does (Q-4, Q-6)."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"p95 latency of GET /api/invoices/overdue ≤ 1000 ms with 10,000 invoices and 50,000 reminder_history rows, with or without filters","text":"The overdue list endpoint responds quickly enough with realistic data volumes."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"The email sender call times out after at most 15 s; POST /api/invoices/{id}/reminders returns within 20 s in 100% of cases, and a timeout is recorded as 'failed'","text":"A reminder send cannot hang indefinitely on the email sender."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"0 customer billing email addresses or reminder email bodies found in application log output across the whole automated test suite run","text":"Customer PII (billing email addresses) and email bodies are kept out of application logs."},{"id":"NFR-4","metric":"100% of the endpoints under /api/invoices return 401 when no valid token is sent (checked by an automated test over the list of endpoints)","text":"All invoice reminder endpoints require authentication."}],"outOfScope":["Payments, and recording payments (the request says so); paid/cancelled status is only read from the existing system (Q-4)","Customer logins and any screens for customers","SMS reminders","Finding delivery failures after hand-off, such as bounces, provider webhooks or later rejections (ASM-13); only errors returned when the email is handed to the email sender count","Guarding against repeat sends beyond disabling the button while a send is in progress (Q-5): no cooldown, daily limit or server-side duplicate check","Editing or deleting reminder history entries (Q-3)","Creating or editing invoices, customers or billing emails; this app only reads them (ASM-1)","Sending to more than one contact per customer (Q-2)","Automatic or scheduled reminders; every send is started by staff","Role-based permissions beyond 'any authenticated staff user' (Q-1)","Configurable email templates or wording (ASM-9, ASM-15)"],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"The threshold is left at the default, the business time zone is Europe/London, and an open invoice is due 2026-09-01","id":"AC-1.1","level":"unit","then":"Days overdue is 6 and the invoice is not overdue","when":"OverduePolicy is evaluated with the current instant 2026-09-07T22:30Z (23:30 on 7 Sep local time)"},{"given":"The same invoice and settings as AC-1.1","id":"AC-1.2","level":"unit","then":"Days overdue is 7 and the invoice is overdue","when":"OverduePolicy is evaluated with the current instant 2026-09-07T23:30Z (00:30 on 8 Sep local time)"},{"given":"The overdue threshold is set to 10 and an open invoice's due date was 8 days ago","id":"AC-1.3","level":"unit","then":"The invoice is not overdue","when":"OverduePolicy is evaluated"},{"given":"An open invoice due 6 days ago is not on the overdue list, and no job or data change runs","id":"AC-1.4","level":"api","then":"The invoice is now in the response with daysOverdue = 7","when":"The injected clock moves forward 1 day and GET /api/invoices/overdue is called again"}],"ears":"The invoice reminders system shall treat an invoice as overdue when the number of calendar days from its due date to today's date, both taken in the configured business time zone, is at least the configured overdue threshold (default 7), working this out each time it is requested rather than storing it.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-6","ASM-2","ASM-10","ASM-11"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The existing database has invoice A (open, due 10 days ago), invoice B (paid, due 20 days ago), invoice C (cancelled, due 15 days ago) and invoice D (open, due 3 days ago)","id":"AC-2.1","level":"api","then":"The response is 200 and contains only invoice A, with daysOverdue = 10 and its invoice number, customer name, amount and due date","when":"GET /api/invoices/overdue is called as an authenticated staff user"},{"given":"Invoice A is on the overdue list","id":"AC-2.2","level":"api","then":"Invoice A is no longer in the response","when":"Its status in the existing invoices table is changed to paid and GET /api/invoices/overdue is called again"}],"ears":"When an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list, the invoice reminders system shall return every overdue invoice whose status in the existing system is not paid or cancelled, and for each one include the invoice ID, invoice number, customer name, amount, due date, days overdue and latest reminder status.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-4","ASM-1","ASM-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Overdue invoice INV-1042 for £245.50 due 2026-09-01 belongs to a customer with billing email accounts@example-cafe.test, and a fake email sender is configured","id":"AC-3.1","level":"api","then":"The response is 2xx, and the fake sender records exactly one message to accounts@example-cafe.test from the configured sender address, whose body contains 'INV-1042', '£245.50' and the due date 2026-09-01","when":"POST /api/invoices/{id}/reminders is called as an authenticated staff user"}],"ears":"When an authenticated staff user sends a reminder for an overdue invoice whose customer has a billing email, the invoice reminders system shall send one email through the configured email sender to that customer's billing email, from the configured sender address, using the fixed template that contains the invoice number, the amount in the local currency, and the due date.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","Q-2","ASM-9","ASM-12","ASM-15"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An overdue invoice whose customer's billing email is null or empty, and a fake email sender","id":"AC-4.1","level":"api","then":"The response is 422 with an error saying the billing email is missing, the fake sender records no message, and one reminder_history row exists for the invoice with status 'failed' and a reason saying the billing email is missing","when":"POST /api/invoices/{id}/reminders is called as an authenticated staff user"}],"ears":"If a staff user sends a reminder for an invoice whose customer has no billing email in the existing record, then the invoice reminders system shall send no email, return an error saying the billing email is missing, and record the attempt as failed.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-2","Q-8","ASM-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An open invoice due 3 days ago (threshold 7) and a paid invoice due 30 days ago","id":"AC-5.1","level":"api","then":"Both responses are 409, the fake sender records no message, and there are no reminder_history rows for either invoice","when":"POST /api/invoices/{id}/reminders is called for each one as an authenticated staff user"}],"ears":"If a staff user sends a reminder for an invoice that is not overdue, including a paid or cancelled invoice, then the invoice reminders system shall send no email, add no reminder history entry, and return a 409 error.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","Q-4","ASM-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Staff user 'jane' is authenticated, an overdue invoice has a customer billing email, and the fake sender succeeds","id":"AC-6.1","level":"api","then":"One reminder_history row exists with that invoice ID, sent_by = jane's user ID, sent_at = the known time in UTC, status = 'sent' and no failure reason","when":"POST /api/invoices/{id}/reminders is called at a known clock time"},{"given":"The same invoice already has one 'sent' row","id":"AC-6.2","level":"api","then":"There are two rows for the invoice, and the new one has sent_by = raj's user ID","when":"Staff user 'raj' sends another reminder"}],"ears":"When a reminder send attempt finishes, the invoice reminders system shall add one row to the reminder history table in the application's Postgres database, holding the invoice ID, the ID of the authenticated staff user who sent it, the server timestamp in UTC, the outcome (sent or failed), and the failure reason when there is one.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","Q-7","Q-8","ASM-6"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An invoice with one reminder_history entry","id":"AC-7.1","level":"api","then":"Each response is 404 or 405, and the entry's columns are unchanged in the database","when":"PUT, PATCH and DELETE requests are sent to /api/invoices/{id}/reminders and /api/invoices/{id}/reminders/{reminderId} as an authenticated staff user"}],"ears":"The invoice reminders system shall not let anyone edit or delete a reminder history entry through its API.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-3"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An overdue invoice whose history has a 'failed' entry at 10:00 and then a 'sent' entry at 10:05","id":"AC-8.1","level":"api","then":"The response has the amount and due date, a history of 2 entries with the 10:05 'sent' entry first, the failed entry including its failure reason, and latestReminderStatus = 'sent'","when":"GET /api/invoices/{id} is called as an authenticated staff user"},{"given":"An overdue invoice with no reminder history","id":"AC-8.2","level":"api","then":"The history is an empty list and latestReminderStatus is null","when":"GET /api/invoices/{id} is called"}],"ears":"When an authenticated staff user requests an invoice's details, the invoice reminders system shall return the invoice number, customer name, amount, due date, whether it is overdue, days overdue, the full reminder history (newest first, each entry with sender, timestamp, outcome and failure reason), and the latest reminder status taken from the newest history entry.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","I-7","Q-8"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An overdue invoice with a customer billing email, and a fake email sender set up to throw a send error 'SMTP 554 rejected'","id":"AC-9.1","level":"api","then":"The response is 502 with an error saying the send failed, a reminder_history row exists with status 'failed' and a reason containing 'SMTP 554 rejected', GET /api/invoices/{id} returns latestReminderStatus = 'failed', and GET /api/invoices/overdue still contains the invoice","when":"POST /api/invoices/{id}/reminders is called as an authenticated staff user"}],"ears":"If the email sender returns an error when a reminder is handed to it, then the invoice reminders system shall return an error response, record the attempt as failed with the sender's error message as the reason, and keep the invoice on the overdue list.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-4","Q-8","ASM-13"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Overdue invoices exist for customer X (2 invoices) and customer Y (1 invoice)","id":"AC-10.1","level":"api","then":"The response contains exactly the 2 invoices for customer X","when":"GET /api/invoices/overdue?customerId={X} is called"}],"ears":"When the overdue list is requested with a customer filter, the invoice reminders system shall return only the overdue invoices that belong to that customer.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Open overdue invoices with days overdue 7, 30, 31, 60, 61 and 90","id":"AC-11.1","level":"api","then":"7-30 returns the invoices at 7 and 30, 31-60 returns those at 31 and 60, and 61+ returns those at 61 and 90","when":"GET /api/invoices/overdue is called with each bucket (7-30, 31-60, 61+) in turn"},{"given":"The same invoices, where only the 31-day and 90-day invoices belong to customer X","id":"AC-11.2","level":"api","then":"Only the 31-day invoice is returned","when":"GET /api/invoices/overdue?customerId={X}&daysOverdue=31-60 is called"}],"ears":"When the overdue list is requested with a days-overdue bucket filter, the invoice reminders system shall return only the overdue invoices whose days overdue fall in that bucket, where the buckets are threshold to 30, 31 to 60, and 61 or more.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","ASM-3","ASM-4"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"No authentication token, or an expired one","id":"AC-12.1","level":"api","then":"Each response is 401, the fake sender records no message, and no reminder_history row is added","when":"GET /api/invoices/overdue, GET /api/invoices/{id} and POST /api/invoices/{id}/reminders are called"},{"given":"A valid token for any staff user who has no special role","id":"AC-12.2","level":"api","then":"The request succeeds (2xx)","when":"POST /api/invoices/{id}/reminders is called for an overdue invoice with a billing email"}],"ears":"If a request to any invoice reminders endpoint has no valid authentication from the existing API, then the invoice reminders system shall return 401, send no email and change no data.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-1"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in staff user and seeded overdue invoices for two customers","id":"AC-13.1","level":"ui","then":"The table shows only matching rows with the listed columns, every row has a 'Send reminder' button, and clicking an invoice number opens that invoice's detail screen","when":"The person opens the overdue list, picks one customer and then the 31-60 bucket"}],"ears":"The overdue list screen shall show the overdue invoices in a table with the invoice number, customer, amount, due date, days overdue and latest reminder status, plus a customer filter, a days-overdue bucket filter, a 'Send reminder' button on each row, and a link from each invoice number to its detail screen.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-6","I-5","ASM-7"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in staff user on the overdue list, with the email sender slowed to take 5 seconds","id":"AC-14.1","level":"ui","then":"The button is disabled until the send finishes, only one reminder_history row is added, and afterwards the row shows the outcome and the button can be pressed again","when":"The person presses 'Send reminder' on a row and tries to press it again straight away"},{"given":"The email sender is set up to fail","id":"AC-14.2","level":"ui","then":"An error message saying the send failed is shown and the invoice stays in the table with latest status 'failed'","when":"The person presses 'Send reminder'"}],"ears":"While a reminder send for an invoice is in progress, the invoice reminders front end shall disable the 'Send reminder' button for that invoice, then enable it again and show the result (sent, or the error message) once the send finishes.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-5","I-4","ASM-14"]},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An overdue invoice with one failed attempt followed by one successful attempt","id":"AC-15.1","level":"ui","then":"The amount, due date and both history entries are shown newest first, the failed entry shows its reason and is marked as a failure, the latest status shows 'sent', and a 'Send reminder' button is shown","when":"A signed-in staff user opens its detail screen"},{"given":"An invoice that is not overdue (due 2 days ago)","id":"AC-15.2","level":"ui","then":"No 'Send reminder' button is shown","when":"A signed-in staff user opens its detail screen"}],"ears":"The invoice detail screen shall show the invoice's number, amount, due date, reminder history (sender, time, outcome, failure reason, newest first), the latest reminder status with delivery failures marked, and a 'Send reminder' button only while the invoice is overdue.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-7","I-3","I-4","ASM-8","ASM-14"]}],"suggestions":["Decide between ASM-5 and ASM-13. If later bounces need to count as delivery failures, add a provider webhook that adds a 'bounced' history entry and updates the latest status.","Think about a server-side guard against duplicate sends, such as rejecting a second send for the same invoice within N minutes. Today the only guard is disabling the button (Q-5), which doesn't cover two staff members or two open tabs.","Think about a database-level guard (revoke UPDATE/DELETE, or add a trigger) so reminder_history stays append-only even outside the API.","Show the configured threshold and bucket boundaries on the overdue list screen so staff know what 'overdue' means.","Give the overdue list pagination and sorting (for example by days overdue) if invoice numbers grow past a few hundred."]}],"models":["claude-opus-5-5","claude-opus-5-5","claude-opus-5-5"],"notes":["No OpenAI key: specify-other ran on claude-opus-5-5 (same family as the implementer)"]}